The docs for `multiple_of` state, "Let the compiler knows that the values in input are all multiples of value.", which I believe is wrong, and made its usage in the matmul implementation very confusing. After digging in the code a bit, I found this, much better, documentation in `AxisInfo.h`:

```
  /// The _divisibility_ information maps the `d`-th
  /// dimension to the largest power-of-two that
  /// divides the first element of all the values along it
  /// For example:
  /// [10, 11, 12, 13, 18, 19, 20, 21]
  /// [20, 21, 22, 23, 28, 29, 30, 31]
  //  would have divisibility [1, 2]
  //  and
  /// [12, 16, 20, 24]
  /// [13, 17, 21, 25]
  /// [14, 18, 22, 26]
  /// [15, 19, 23, 27]
  //  would have divisibility [4, 1]
```

Can we copy this description to the public API and document `max_contiguous` similarly?

